In the dense jungles of Stranglethorn Vale, a diminutive Gnome Warlock named Gizmok the Shadowbound trudged through the underbrush, his diminutive frame barely noticeable amidst the towering ferns. His loyal Succubus, Lilith, slithered gracefully beside him, her crimson eyes scanning the shadows for danger.

As they approached a clearing, Gizmok sensed a group of Venture Co. goons lurking nearby. With a flick of his wrist, he summoned a Fel Fireball, while Lilith's Lash of Pain lashed out, striking the nearest foe. The goons, caught off guard, struggled to retaliate as Lilith's Seduction ensnared one, leaving him dazed and helpless. Gizmok grinned, his eyes gleaming with mischief, as he and his pet made quick work of the remaining enemies.

Despite the ease of their victory, Gizmok couldn't help but wonder why so many of his fellow Warlocks preferred the Voidwalker over Lilith. She was faster, more agile, and her crowd control abilities made questing a breeze. Yet, the Voidwalker's reputation as a tanky, dependable companion seemed to hold sway.

---

**Answer:** Most Warlocks use Voidwalkers because they are seen as more reliable and tanky companions, despite the Succubus being generally better for leveling and questing due to its superior damage output and crowd control abilities. [end of text]


